course: dictionary
lesson: 3227
title: Enthusiastic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enthusiastic means very interested, excited and keen about something. Look at the words around it to find the clues. «The enthusiastic crowd cheered every goal.» Cheering every goal shows the crowd is excited and keen, so enthusiastic must mean full of energy and happy about the game.
explain: You can use enthusiastic with a person or a thing. You can be enthusiastic about a hobby, like «enthusiastic about football». You can also give an enthusiastic welcome, which means a warm, lively welcome full of energy.
explain: Teachers sometimes write «an enthusiastic learner» on school reports to praise a pupil who joins in eagerly. Read the whole report to understand it, because the words around the phrase show what the teacher really means.
fact: Enthusiastic means very interested, excited and keen.
fact: Enthusiastic also means showing lots of energy and happiness when you do something.
fact: Keen is a close synonym for enthusiastic, but enthusiastic often sounds more lively and full of energy.
fact: You can say enthusiastic about something, as in «She was enthusiastic about painting».
fact: The opposite of enthusiastic is bored or uninterested.
exercise: «The enthusiastic crowd cheered every goal.» What does enthusiastic mean? | *Very excited and keen | Bored and sleepy | Very quiet | Angry at the referee
exercise: Mia's teacher wrote: «Mia is an enthusiastic learner.» What does this tell us? | Mia never comes to school | *Mia really likes learning and wants to join in | Mia has learned to shout | Mia is ill today
exercise: Which word means the opposite of enthusiastic? | Eager | *Bored | Excited | Keen
test: Which sentence shows someone is enthusiastic? | Ravi stared at the clock all lesson | *Ravi shot up his hand, eager to answer the question | Ravi yawned and put his head down on the desk | Ravi left the room without a word
test: Which sentence uses enthusiastic correctly? | The enthusiastic book was on the shelf | The enthusiastic rain fell all afternoon | The enthusiastic table was made of wood | *The enthusiastic puppy raced across the park to meet us
exam: Read: «Josh is an enthusiastic contributor.» What does this most likely mean? | Josh is unhappy and quiet in class | Josh is always late for lessons | Josh never speaks at all | *Josh loves joining in and is keen to share his ideas
